    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `capacityWarning` flag follows the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern \u2014 a per-response derived flag attached in `buildOwnerDto`, so it's returned on both create and read without any schema/entity changes.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` boolean to the `OwnerDto` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time, giving it a `setCapacityWarning` setter).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - `buildOwnerDto` now sets `capacityWarning` via a new `isCapacityWarning(owner)` helper.\n   - `isCapacityWarning` returns true when the count of **other** owners already in the owner's city is in `[40, 49]`.\n   - Added `countOtherOwnersInCity(owner)` \u2014 same case-insensitive/whitespace-collapsed city matching as `countOwnersInCity`, but excluding the owner itself.\n\n## Why count *other* owners\n\nI excluded the owner being read so the basis exactly mirrors the hard 50-gate (`countOwnersInCity(...) >= 50`), which counts the owners *already present* before the new one is added. This makes the warning true precisely when \"the owner's city already has between 40 and 49 owners\":\n- The 41st owner in a city \u2192 40 pre-existing \u2192 warns \u2713 (this is what the test asserts).\n- The owner that takes a city from 49\u219250 \u2192 49 pre-existing \u2192 still warns (49 \u2208 [40,49]), correctly right up to the limit.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 is untouched.",
